--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SettingsPage.tsx is the application-preferences screen. It calls useSettings()
ONLY for its `isLoading` flag (the `<PageContainer title subtitle loading={isLoading}>`
overlay), claims an edit lease for `settings/general`, and renders, in order: the
find-as-you-type box <SettingsSearch/>, the cross-tab <EditConflictBanner
resourceKey="settings/general" resourceLabel={t('editConflict.resource.settings')}/>,
the four preference sections (<GeneralSettings/>, <AppearanceSettings/>,
<AdvancedSettings/>, <ResetSection/>), and three link/action GlassPanels — a Data
Export link card (<a href="/data-export">, Download + ExternalLink glyphs), an
Onboarding Tour card (PlayCircle glyph + a button calling dispatchTourLauncherOpen()),
and a Setup Checklist card (Rocket glyph + a button calling restartChecklist() +
toast.success(t('checklist.settings.restarted'))).

The manifest scopes this page's parity to the three GlassPanels (GlassPanel1/2/3),
the loading -> success states of useSettings, and 12 i18n strings; the four preference
sections are separately-tracked A3 component units and are composed here for fidelity.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no skeletons, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The four web sections already exist as A3 feature-views
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.{generalsettings,appearancesettings,
advancedsettings,resetsection}.*) and the search box / edit-conflict banner / tour
launcher as shared surfaces; this page composes them and adds the three cards + the
PageContainer-equivalent chrome, exactly as the sibling A7 pages reuse their A3
feature-views (ArchivedPage reuses InboxBody).

The `settings` / `/settings` destination already existed in Destinations.kt, hosted
by the temporary A8 native-settings seam (io.teslasync.android.settings.SettingsPageHost),
whose own doc said it stood in "until A7 wires its generated pages". This A7 host now
owns that route; TeslaSyncApplication's import + registration were swapped from the A8
host to the A7 host. A7 files live in package io.teslasync.android.settings.page (dir
kotlin/com/teslasync/settings) so they never clash with the A8 io.teslasync.android.settings
package; the A8 native screen remains in the repo, no longer wired to /settings.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.settings.page):
  - SettingsPageModel.kt      SettingsPageRegistration (ROUTE_ID settings, WEB_PATH
                              /settings, DATA_EXPORT_PATH /data-export, LEASE_KEY
                              settings/general, SLUG SettingsPage) + recordSettingsPageOpened.
  - SettingsPageSource.kt     SettingsPageSource seam + settingsPageSourceOf(settingsStore):
                              the `GET /settings` document feed (web useSettings).
  - SettingsPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; state: StateFlow<UiState<JsonElement>>
                              via source.settings().asUiState(isEmpty = { false })
                              (Loading -> Content); recordViewOpened (one-shot view.opened).
  - SettingsPageGlyphs.kt     Locally-authored lucide-style Download / PlayCircle /
                              Rocket / ExternalLink stroked ImageVectors.
  - SettingsPage.kt           Stateful entry (viewModel factory) + stateful overload
                              (collectAsStateWithLifecycle, deep-link + toast + tour
                              seams, SettingsPageActions, mounts the page-local
                              TourLauncher modal) + stateless SettingsPageContent
                              (header always visible; loading-spinner <-> body switch =
                              the web PageContainer loading contract; SettingsSearch +
                              EditConflictBanner + GeneralSettings + AppearanceSettings +
                              AdvancedSettings + ResetSection + the three cards) +
                              DataExportCard / OnboardingTourCard / SetupChecklistCard +
                              openRoute (teslasync://app/... ACTION_VIEW deep-link).
  - SettingsPageHost.kt       SettingsPageRoute() binds container.settingsStore +
                              a page-local SettingsResetStore(HttpSettingsResetRepository(
                              api, cacheStore)) + a device-local
                              SharedPreferencesConfirmSilenceStore(context);
                              SettingsPageHost.register() -> PageHosts.register("settings").

Edits (registration + string catalog + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt   import swap io.teslasync.android.settings.SettingsPageHost
                              -> io.teslasync.android.settings.page.SettingsPageHost (A7
                              supersedes the A8 seam at process start).
  - res/values/strings.xml    2 keys: translation_settings_title ("Settings") +
                              translation_settings_subtitle. The other 10 keys already
                              existed (translation_checklist_settings_*, translation_export_*,
                              translation_tour_*, translation_editConflict_resource_settings).
                              The bare `title`/`subtitle` keys are owned by another namespace
                              in the flattened catalog (translation_title="Command Center"),
                              so the page-namespaced settings_title/subtitle were added.
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:settings/Settings row (done, 17/17).

Notes:
  - Navigation: page hosts get no LocalNavController (GlancePage/ArchivedPage precedent),
    so the Data-Export link (web <a href="/data-export">) and SettingsSearch
    navigate(entry.route) hand the route's teslasync://app/... deep-link URI to an
    ACTION_VIEW Intent — the shell's own deep-link mechanism.
  - Tour: the web app-level launcher modal is popped by a global event; with no app-level
    mount the page hosts its own rememberTourLauncherController + TourLauncher modal, so the
    card button opens a real launcher (tour list, completion state, reset-all all wired).
    Replaying a tour is owned by the separate tour-player unit, so onStartTour records the
    intent and the launcher closes itself (no fabricated playback).
  - Checklist: the restart raises the web confirmation toast (translation_checklist_settings_
    restarted) via the shared LocalToastController and logs the intent; the persistent
    checklist flags are owned by the OnboardingChecklistWidget unit's preferences.
  - SI: no field on this page is unit-bearing (the document is read only for isLoading; the
    composed sections convert at their own display boundary), so no SI conversion here (S5).
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept. MissingTranslation
    is disabled in build.gradle.kts (ar/he ship English fallback), so the 2 new keys are en-only.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading + BodyText subtitle; the Data-Export panel is a clickable target with an
    onClickLabel; the card glyphs are decorative (null contentDescription, the title/label carries
    meaning); Buttons carry their localized labels (ADR-015).

